Task 1: Explore RHACM Components - Hub Cluster
Subtask 1.1: Understanding the Hub Cluster Architecture
The Hub cluster serves as the central management point for all managed clusters in your RHACM environment. Let's explore its components and functionality.

Step 1: Access the Hub Cluster
Connect to your Hub cluster using the provided credentials:

# Set the Hub cluster context
export KUBECONFIG=/home/student/hub-cluster-kubeconfig

# Verify connection to Hub cluster
oc whoami
oc cluster-info
Step 2: Examine RHACM Operator Installation
Check the RHACM operator installation and its components:

# List RHACM related namespaces
oc get namespaces | grep -E "(open-cluster-management|multicluster)"

# Check the RHACM operator status
oc get csv -n open-cluster-management -o wide

# Examine the MultiClusterHub custom resource
oc get multiclusterhub -n open-cluster-management -o yaml
Step 3: Explore Hub Cluster Components
Investigate the core components running on the Hub cluster:

# List all pods in the open-cluster-management namespace
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management

# Check the cluster-manager deployment
oc describe deployment cluster-manager -n open-cluster-management

# Examine the application lifecycle components
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management-addon-manager
Subtask 1.2: Analyzing Hub Cluster Services
Step 4: Examine Core Services
# List services in the RHACM namespace
